{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== THE OUTBOUND HALF IS PROVEN LIVE. THE EPIC'S HEADLINE AC NOW HAS EVIDENCE IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. ===\n\nEVIDENCE. GitHub Actions run 30716856124, job 91413789980 (\"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data\nCenter, ephemeral)\"), main @ 2c9c9843f. Result: **1 failed, 25 passed in 534.56s**. The verdict that\nmatters:\n\n  PASSED tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py::test_a_local_edit_reaches_the_dc_issue_outbound\n\nThat is the cell this story exists to turn green, and it did so against a real Data Center instance.\n\nWHY THIS GREEN CARRIES INFORMATION — I checked the oracle before accepting its verdict, per the\nstanding rule that an unexamined GREEN is worth no more than an unexamined RED.\n  * It writes a UNIQUE value: `new_title = f\"rebar J11 outbound proof {key}\"`. No pre-existing DC\n    summary can equal it, so the assertion cannot be satisfied by a stale read.\n  * It reads back FROM THE INSTANCE, not from local state: `dc_transport.get_issue_by_rest(key)`\n    then asserts `fields.summary == new_title`. The value asserted is the value this cell wrote —\n    a genuine round-trip, not a re-read of an unchanged field.\n  * Its `bound_dc_issue` fixture ASSERTS THE BINDING BEFORE YIELDING\n    (`get_jira_key(local_id) == key`). This closes the exact false-green this epic has been bitten\n    by: without a binding, `outbound_differ.py:518-520` routes the ticket to CREATE, and the oracle\n    would then pass against a freshly created issue while proving nothing about the edit path.\n  * The pass is SCOPED with `--filter-local-ids {local_id},{key}`, so the 1600+ unbound creates the\n    scrub produces cannot fire and cannot contaminate the result.\nA vacuous pass would therefore require the DC issue to already carry a title naming this run's key.\nIt cannot.\n\nTHE ONE REMAINING FAILURE IS ALREADY FIXED AND IN REVIEW — it is NOT an outbound defect.\n`test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed` failed with:\n  assert {'.ensure-app...9b-4daa', ...} == {'003a-09ae-9...d4-4c47', ...}\ni.e. the copied set now contains `.ensure-*` marker dot-files that the baseline set does not. That\nis the exact defect Gerrit change 1177 (\"5200: count tickets structurally, pin the baseline\")\nrepairs — filter store entries STRUCTURALLY rather than by an enumerated dot-file list, and pin the\nbaseline commit instead of re-sampling a LIVE tickets branch at assertion time. Both halves of that\nfailure were predicted in this epic's standing rules before the run produced it.\n\nSTATUS OF THE 26 CELLS: 25 green, 1 red for a test-harness bookkeeping reason with its fix in\nreview. Nothing in the failing cell touches the inbound or outbound apply paths.\n\nNEXT: land 1177, re-run the harness, and expect 26/26. The epic's closing condition — \"an issue\ncreated in DC appears locally; a local edit appears in DC\" — is satisfied on the evidence above;\nthe re-run is confirmation that the whole suite is green, not the outbound proof itself."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785618117928100001,"uuid":"6b12e26c-6753-4ec9-878e-a57f0f06b00e"}